--TEST--
`Core\Socket::upgrade`'s entry is a sink, so a path that came from outside the program cannot select what a connection runs — `rule:concurrency/an-upgrade-is-spawn-shaped`, `rule:http-server/a-path-is-never-derived-from-a-url`
--ARGS--
sockets/chat.nvs
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The entry's content becomes the instruction "execute this file", which is
// `rule:security/sink-predicate`'s definition of a sink, and `rule:http-server/a-path-is-never-derived-from-a-url` is the same rule
// written for the server: a filesystem path is never *constructed* at request
// time, only selected from a set enumerated before the request arrived. An
// upgrade is a request-time call, so a word that arrived from outside is shut
// out here even though it names a file that exists.
foreach (Core\Cli::arguments() as tainted string $word) {
    Core\Socket::upgrade($word);
    echo "unreachable\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:9:26
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
